{"diagnosis": "Loopback with divider 64 sent 0xa5 but read back 0x00, causing TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0x00 want 0xa5 and tohost FAIL 0xdead (picosoc/simpleuart.v:20, picosoc/picosoc.v:124). Root cause in excerpt is line 72 which resets recv_buf_valid to 1 instead of 0, marking empty recv_buf_data (0) as valid. Thus reg_dat_do at line 53 returns stale 0x00 on first read instead of waiting for the real RX byte.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -66,10 +66,10 @@
 	always @(posedge clk) begin
 		if (!resetn) begin
 			recv_state <= 0;
 			recv_divcnt <= 0;
 			recv_pattern <= 0;
 			recv_buf_data <= 0;
-			recv_buf_valid <= 1;
+			recv_buf_valid <= 0;
 		end else begin
 			recv_divcnt <= recv_divcnt + 1;
 			if (reg_dat_re)
", "expected": "tohost PASS (was FAIL 0xdead), TRAP gone, uart loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5"}

